{"id":"chatcmpl-7661ac5d-ae4d-4dcb-9ca8-a491c8672a07","object":"chat.completion","created":1795244634,"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","reasoning_content":"","content":"```json\n{\n  \"highlights\": \"This task demonstrates a two-stage verification strategy for spatial/positional questions in medical imaging: first identify the presence and location of the finding via a domain expert tool, then independently confirm laterality using a grounded coordinate/report tool. The key insight is cross-checking the qualitative answer against coordinate-based evidence and radiological convention (image-left = patient-right) before committing to an answer. This pattern generalizes to any task requiring side/location disambiguation where tools provide complementary qualitative and quantitative evidence.\",\n  \"patterns\": [\n    \"For laterality or side-of-body questions, first query a domain expert for presence and side, then independently verify with a coordinate/grounding tool before answering.\",\n    \"When tools return spatial coordinates, translate them using domain convention (e.g., image-left corresponds to patient-right) rather than assuming screen orientation matches anatomical orientation.\",\n    \"Decompose binary location questions into two sub-queries: (1) is the finding present, and (2) on which side — resolving presence before committing to a side reduces misclassification.\",\n    \"Use a second, independent tool as a cross-check when the first tool's answer is qualitative; agreement between qualitative and quantitative evidence justifies the final answer.\"\n  ],\n  \"playbooks\": {\n    \"Medical imaging interpretation\": \"Always confirm laterality against radiological convention (image-left = patient-right); pair an expert-read tool with a coordinate/grounding tool for independent verification.\",\n    \"Spatial/location disambiguation tasks\": \"Separate 'presence' from 'position' queries; use coordinates or bounding boxes to validate the qualitative side/location claim.\",\n    \"Multi-tool evidence fusion\": \"When two tools provide complementary evidence types (qualitative vs. quantitative), require agreement before finalizing; cite the coordinate evidence in the rationale.\"\n  },\n  \"checklists\": [\n    \"Confirm the finding is present before deciding its side/location.\",\n    \"Verify laterality using coordinates or a second tool, applying the correct image-to-anatomy orientation convention.\"\n  ]\n}\n```"},"finish_reason":"stop","logprobs":null}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":460,"total_tokens":885,"completion_tokens":425,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":460},"completion_tokens_details":{"text_tokens":425}}}